1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,060
 This is why AI beats you at trading.

2
00:00:02,120 --> 00:00:04,220
 AI trading beats you in three ways.

3
00:00:04,400 --> 00:00:06,360
 And the last one can wipe out your account.

4
00:00:06,580 --> 00:00:07,660
 One, it doesn't panic.

5
00:00:07,800 --> 00:00:10,180
 You lose a trade three times in a row and you get angry.

6
00:00:10,260 --> 00:00:11,280
 You start a revenge trade.

7
00:00:11,380 --> 00:00:12,960
 That's how people blow up their accounts.

8
00:00:13,120 --> 00:00:15,060
 AI just follow the rules.

9
00:00:15,280 --> 00:00:16,220
 Two, it doesn't sleep.

10
00:00:16,380 --> 00:00:18,060
 You can watch 304 charts.

11
00:00:18,240 --> 00:00:21,160
 AI can watch every chart, all day and all night.

12
00:00:21,240 --> 00:00:25,700
 Three, it can test thousands of strategies on usable prices in seconds.

13
00:00:25,880 --> 00:00:27,000
 That's called a backtest.

14
00:00:27,120 --> 00:00:28,200
 Sounds perfect, right?

15
00:00:28,300 --> 00:00:29,320
 But here's the problem.

16
00:00:29,320 --> 00:00:33,820
 If you test thousands of strategies, some of them will look good just because of luck.

17
00:00:33,920 --> 00:00:34,860
 Think about it like this.

18
00:00:34,940 --> 00:00:37,540
 Get a thousand people to flip a coin 10 times.

19
00:00:37,620 --> 00:00:39,800
 And one of them will get a heads up all 10 times.

20
00:00:39,980 --> 00:00:41,700
 That person doesn't have a magic coin.

21
00:00:41,860 --> 00:00:42,580
 They just got lucky.

22
00:00:42,780 --> 00:00:46,860
 Researchers checked this with 888 real trading strategies.

23
00:00:47,040 --> 00:00:53,020
 And how good a strategy did in the past tells you almost nothing about how it would do in the future.

24
00:00:53,200 --> 00:00:57,000
 So the more strategy AI tests, the more lucky ones have found.

25
00:00:57,120 --> 00:00:57,760
 Here's the fix.

26
00:00:57,760 --> 00:01:01,600
 Build your strategies on older years, like 2015 to 20.

27
00:01:01,720 --> 00:01:05,180
 Then test it on years that it has never seen, like 21 to now.

28
00:01:05,260 --> 00:01:07,140
 If it still works, you might have something.

29
00:01:07,240 --> 00:01:09,540
 If it falls apart, it might just be a lucky coin.

30
00:01:09,760 --> 00:01:11,660
 Common Q, and I'll send you the full breakdown.

